Cell["\<\
Source and drain must be the first and final leads. The source comments \
describe lead order from left to right and from top to bottom for four-, \
five- and six-terminal layouts.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->462244440,ExpressionUUID->"a730968f-b104-b243-9177-0fb4d8a5ffc1"],

Cell["\<\
All lead self-energies act on the final device layer. Options are \"SigmaMode\
\" -> 3, \"SigmaTransform\" -> Identity, and \"GreenTransform\" -> Identity.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1457804691,ExpressionUUID->"08ade69b-4494-8646-a9e0-b4f0f7701b01"],

Cell["\<\
Returns {RH, RL}; the code returns {\"NaN\", \"NaN\"} when its condition \
estimate exceeds 1.*^7.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1603288228,ExpressionUUID->"28d64328-feee-7540-9626-403d464af153"],

Cell["\<\
The implementation reads the fourth part of LUDecomposition[matrix]. \
Compatibility with kernels returning a three-part decomposition must be \
checked. The example is a small ring fixture, not a realistic Hall-bar \
geometry.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1703753091,ExpressionUUID->"a8063f49-2b9a-d54a-bafa-40ba4aab071b"]
}, Closed]],

